# GQuay Tier 1 secrets.
#
# These cannot live in GitHub. The REST API lists Actions *secrets* without
# revealing their values — by design, and only a workflow runtime can decrypt
# one. The Router is a standalone process, not an Actions job, so a value it
# cannot read back is a value it cannot use. Actions *Variables* are different
# and are read live; see docs/06-configuration.md for the four-tier split.
#
# Copy to .env and chmod 600.

# ── Claude ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set EXACTLY ONE of the two below. Claude Code resolves credentials in a fixed
# order and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ranks ABOVE CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — under `-p`
# the key is used whenever present, without prompting. So a leftover API key
# silently bills every session to the Console org while the subscription token
# sits unused, with no error to notice. An empty ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="" still wins
# its slot; it has to be genuinely unset (comment the line out).
#
# `gquay doctor` reports which one will actually be used, and the Router logs it
# at boot.

# Option A — Claude subscription (Pro / Max / Team / Enterprise).
# Generate with `claude setup-token`: it opens the normal browser authorization,
# then prints a one-year OAuth token to the terminal. It is NOT saved anywhere —
# copy it here. Right for personal automation on your own repositories.
# Note: this is CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, *not* ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN — the latter
# is an LLM-gateway bearer, ranks even higher, and is a different thing entirely.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Option B — Console API key, with its own billing and spend controls.
# Right when GQuay serves a team: it routes other people's requests, and a
# per-seat subscription is not built to sit behind that.
#
# Leave this COMMENTED OUT unless you use it. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` with an
# empty value is not the same as unset — an empty value still wins its
# precedence slot, so sessions authenticate with an empty credential and fail
# while the token above sits ignored. The Router refuses to start rather than
# let that happen quietly.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── GitHub App ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prefer github.private_key_path in router.yml. This is the inline alternative.
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"

# The webhook HMAC secret. Must be known before any GitHub call is trusted.
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Hook Bus ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer for the loopback hook listener. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
HOOK_BUS_TOKEN=

# ── Teams ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Power Automate Workflows trigger URL. The `sig` query parameter is a
# credential, so treat the entire URL as one. Hooks never see this — only the
# Hook Bus holds it.
TEAMS_WORKFLOW_URL=

# ── Dispatch workers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One per dispatch target, matching its worker_token_env in router.yml.
GQUAY_WORKER_TOKEN_KINGSPAN=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GQUAY_LOG_LEVEL=info
# GQUAY_CONFIG=/etc/gquay/router.yml
